    {
      "object_id": "mathia_interpretation_5cca37972ddc05ab4d63862874a1a6c040cf4c855fe8748b2da4ad062e1d7be7",
      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "For COE modulus moments, removing the quadratic growth N^(s²/2) leaves a coefficient obtained by matching the local cumulant series to gamma and Barnes G expansions and continuing the result meromorphically. This remainder carries negative-axis pole data and rational positive-even specializations that would be lost if only the dominant N scaling were kept. The stated degree-2k² polynomial leading term checks the s=2k specialization, while the phase calculation supplies its own zero multiplicities. The unit establishes only this COE mechanism, not a comparison with other ensembles or an L-function model.",
