    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_b94da44fdec5916a0272c7d90ff31907848ea6b98da5882ead08bf96dd6429cd",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The divergent second-cumulant scale suppresses bounded higher cumulants after normalization, while exact vanishing of all odd phase cumulants removes the cubic correction: the phase density is even at every finite N and its leading Gaussian deviation is of order (log N)^(-2), rather than the real part's order (log N)^(-3/2). A joint generator is separately needed to show that normalized mixed terms vanish and the limiting components are independent.",
