    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_f6fe87a99af1bb0842ed2c9c9e7c2cdf9356d0464d9107764731cad278e422ad",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Across CUE, COE, and CSE, logarithmically growing variance with convergent fixed higher cumulants yields the same normalized Gaussian mechanism, but the symmetry parameter remains visible in variance calibration and in the meromorphic remainder after dominant growth is removed. In particular, CSE and COE have different rational moment subsequences and different modulus-pole and phase-zero patterns, so common limiting shape does not imply identical finite-size or special-function structure.",
